<title>USA: Marathon Oil lifts US posted crude $1/bbl.</title>
<headline>Marathon Oil lifts US posted crude $1/bbl.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-10-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Marathon Oil said it raised the price it will pay for U.S. crude oil by $1.00 a barrel, effective today.</p>
<p>The increase brings the new price for U.S. benchmark grade West Texas Intermediate to $24.00 a barrel, and West Texas Sour to $22.65 a barrel.</p>
<p>Light Louisiana sweet crude is now $24.25 a barrel, and Oklahoma sweet is $24.00.</p>
<p>-- New York Energy Desk, +1 212 859-1620</p>
</text>
